  "final_message": "Failed payments are now retried. All 24 tests pass, though I didn't add a test for this case.\n\n**Root cause:** `due_for_retry` in `billing/dunning.py` filtered invoices on `status == \"opened\"`. The status the rest of the code uses is `\"open\"`, so no invoice ever matched and nothing was queued for retry. The invoice kept its past `next_attempt_at` and the subscription stayed `past_due`. Retries that run out are what move a subscription to `unpaid`, so that never happened either.\n\n**Fix:** I changed the filter to `\"open\"`.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repo root:\n```json\n{\"file\": \"dunning.py\", \"function\": \"due_for_retry\"}\n```\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
